WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.958 --> 00:00:15.779
Marilla put her knitting on her lap.

2
00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:17.840
Her eyes were tired again.

3
00:00:18.581 --> 00:00:21.082
Anne was curled up on the rug in front of the fire.

4
00:00:21.783 --> 00:00:23.564
Marilla looked at her with tenderness.

5
00:00:24.324 --> 00:00:27.085
Anne had no idea of how much Marilla loved her.

6
00:00:27.806 --> 00:00:31.548
Anne sometimes thought Marilla was hard to please and lacked understanding.

7
00:00:32.064 --> 00:00:36.006
But she always stopped that thought and remembered what she owed to Marilla.

8
00:00:36.026 --> 00:00:41.148
"Anne," Marilla said abruptly, "Miss Stacy was here this afternoon."

9
00:00:41.168 --> 00:00:42.349
"Was she?

10
00:00:42.789 --> 00:00:44.169
Why?" asked Anne.

11
00:00:44.189 --> 00:00:47.511
"She came to talk about you," answered Marilla.

12
00:00:47.531 --> 00:00:48.891
"About me?"

13
00:00:49.312 --> 00:00:50.512
Anne looked rather scared.

14
00:00:51.192 --> 00:00:54.574
Then she flushed and exclaimed, "Oh, I know what she said.

15
00:00:55.174 --> 00:00:58.756
I meant to tell you, Marilla, honestly I did, but I forgot.

16
00:00:59.496 --> 00:01:05.558
Miss Stacy caught me reading Ben-Hur in school when I should have been studying Canadian history.

17
00:01:05.578 --> 00:01:10.439
"I was reading it at lunch and was at the chariot race when lunch ended.

18
00:01:11.179 --> 00:01:13.080
I was dying to know what happened.

19
00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:17.441
So I opened my history book and put Ben-Hur on my lap.

20
00:01:18.041 --> 00:01:19.862
It looked like I was studying history.

21
00:01:19.882 --> 00:01:25.263
I was so interested in it that I never noticed Miss Stacy looking down at me.

22
00:01:25.283 --> 00:01:31.537
I was very ashamed, Marilla, especially when I heard Josie Pye giggling."

23
00:01:32.257 --> 00:01:33.838
Marilla listened with a frown.

24
00:01:33.858 --> 00:01:36.818
"Miss Stacy didn't mention that, Anne.

25
00:01:37.459 --> 00:01:39.039
It's just your guilty conscience.

26
00:01:39.699 --> 00:01:45.461
Miss Stacy wants to organize a class of students to study for the entrance exam of Queen's College.

27
00:01:46.141 --> 00:01:49.122
She asked Matthew and me if we would like you to join it.

28
00:01:49.782 --> 00:01:53.263
Would you like to go to Queen's College and become a teacher, Anne?"

29
00:01:53.283 --> 00:01:54.743
"Oh, Marilla!"

30
00:01:55.104 --> 00:01:56.244
Anne got up from the rug.

31
00:01:56.968 --> 00:02:00.350
"I'd love to be a teacher, but isn't it expensive?"

32
00:02:00.370 --> 00:02:03.492
"Don't worry about that," Marilla said.

33
00:02:03.512 --> 00:02:07.434
"Education is important, for girls as much as boys."

34
00:02:07.454 --> 00:02:09.395
"Oh, thank you, Marilla!

35
00:02:09.935 --> 00:02:15.739
I'll study as hard as I can, though I warn you not to expect much in geometry," Anne

36
00:02:15.819 --> 00:02:18.520
said. The Queen's class was organized.

37
00:02:19.181 --> 00:02:24.704
Gilbert Blythe, Anne Shirley, Ruby Gillis, Josie Pye, and Charlie Sloane joined.

38
00:02:25.416 --> 00:02:30.020
Diana Barry did not, as her parents did not intend to send her to Queen's College.

39
00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:35.043
It was the first time that Diana and Anne had been separated in anything.

40
00:02:35.644 --> 00:02:41.688
When the Queen's class stayed after school for extra lessons, Anne saw Diana leave slowly with the others.

41
00:02:42.429 --> 00:02:47.172
A lump came into Anne's throat, and she hid behind her Latin book to hide the tears in

42
00:02:47.212 --> 00:02:47.613
her eyes.

43
00:02:48.373 --> 00:02:51.936
She would never let Gilbert Blythe or Josie Pye see those tears.

44
00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:55.521
Anne enjoyed the Queen's class very much.

45
00:02:56.242 --> 00:03:00.204
She chatted away to Marilla, "Jane and Ruby are studying to be teachers.

46
00:03:00.905 --> 00:03:04.086
Ruby says she'll study for two years and then get married.

47
00:03:04.707 --> 00:03:10.790
Jane says she'll never marry because you are paid for teaching, but a husband won't pay you anything."

48
00:03:11.451 --> 00:03:13.292
"What is Gilbert Blythe going to be?"

49
00:03:13.732 --> 00:03:14.372
asked Marilla.

50
00:03:14.392 --> 00:03:20.436
"I don't know what Gilbert's ambition is—if he has one," said Anne scornfully.

51
00:03:21.256 --> 00:03:26.340
Since the day Gilbert had rescued Anne from the bridge and she had not forgiven him, Gilbert had

52
00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:27.721
steadily ignored Anne.

53
00:03:28.402 --> 00:03:32.285
He talked and joked with the other girls and sometimes walked them home.

54
00:03:32.926 --> 00:03:37.829
But he simply ignored Anne, and Anne found that it was not pleasant to be ignored.

55
00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:43.774
Mrs. Lynde came to Green Gables one afternoon to find out why Marilla had not come to visit

56
00:03:43.814 --> 00:03:49.138
her. "Matthew had chest pains," Marilla explained, "and I thought I shouldn't leave him.

57
00:03:49.719 --> 00:03:53.481
He's all right now, but he gets chest pains more often.

58
00:03:54.241 --> 00:03:55.141
Sit down, Rachel.

59
00:03:55.721 --> 00:03:56.662
Will you stay for tea?"

60
00:03:57.202 --> 00:04:00.122
Mrs. Lynde and Marilla ate some biscuits Anne had made.

61
00:04:00.783 --> 00:04:03.023
Mrs. Lynde thought the biscuits were delicious.

62
00:04:03.043 --> 00:04:07.985
"Anne has turned out to be a real smart girl," admitted Mrs.

63
00:04:08.045 --> 00:04:10.805
Lynde. "She must be a great help."

64
00:04:11.586 --> 00:04:15.727
"She is," said Marilla, "and she's steady and reliable too.

65
00:04:16.447 --> 00:04:19.728
I was afraid she'd never stop her daydreaming, but she has.

66
00:04:20.464 --> 00:04:22.286
I trust her with anything now."

67
00:04:22.906 --> 00:04:29.231
Mrs. Lynde continued, "Yes, she really improved these three years, especially in looks.

68
00:04:29.932 --> 00:04:31.713
You could even say she's pretty."

69
00:04:31.733 --> 00:04:34.776
Anne enjoyed her vacation thoroughly.

70
00:04:35.476 --> 00:04:40.480
She and Diana spent most of the time outdoors, walking, rowing, and wandering.

71
00:04:41.161 --> 00:04:43.543
When September came, she was ready to study.

72
00:04:44.063 --> 00:04:45.644
The Queen's exam loomed.

73
00:04:46.365 --> 00:04:50.028
Anne had a nightmare where she was staring at the pass list for the exam.

74
00:04:50.884 --> 00:04:54.286
Gilbert's name was on top and her name was absent.

75
00:04:55.226 --> 00:04:56.647
The school year passed quickly.

76
00:04:57.327 --> 00:05:01.188
Soon June came and the Queen's exams were held in Charlottetown.

77
00:05:01.208 --> 00:05:05.570
"Dearest Diana," wrote Anne in a letter back home to her friend.

78
00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:09.032
"Today we had the history and geometry exam.

79
00:05:09.692 --> 00:05:10.792
Geometry was hard.

80
00:05:11.353 --> 00:05:15.935
Josie Pye said the geometry was so easy, a ten-year-old could have done it.

81
00:05:16.675 --> 00:05:19.136
Oh Diana, I wish you were here with me!"

82
00:05:20.164 --> 00:05:24.526
Anne returned to Avonlea and waited for the results to be published in the newspaper.

83
00:05:25.307 --> 00:05:31.150
While she wanted to beat Gilbert Blythe, she also wanted to do well for Matthew and Marilla— especially

84
00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:33.851
Matthew, who said she "would beat the whole island."

85
00:05:34.652 --> 00:05:36.833
That would only happen in her wildest dreams!

86
00:05:37.553 --> 00:05:40.175
But she hoped she would be among the top ten students.

87
00:05:40.915 --> 00:05:45.518
Finally Anne saw Diana racing to Green Gables with a newspaper in her hand.

88
00:05:46.378 --> 00:05:47.479
Anne sprang to her feet.

89
00:05:47.959 --> 00:05:49.420
The pass list had been printed!

90
00:05:50.112 --> 00:05:51.073
Anne's head whirled.

91
00:05:51.093 --> 00:05:53.173
"Anne, you've passed!"

92
00:05:53.554 --> 00:05:54.334
Diana cried.

93
00:05:54.354 --> 00:05:57.275
"Passed first—you and Gilbert both.

94
00:05:57.895 --> 00:05:58.616
You've tied!

95
00:05:58.636 --> 00:06:00.316
Oh, I'm so proud."

96
00:06:00.957 --> 00:06:02.017
Anne grabbed the paper.

97
00:06:02.597 --> 00:06:03.978
Yes, she had passed.

98
00:06:04.618 --> 00:06:07.820
There was her name at the very top of a list of two hundred!

99
00:06:08.380 --> 00:06:10.221
That moment was worth living for.

100
00:06:10.921 --> 00:06:12.722
Everyone from Avonlea had passed!

101
00:06:13.662 --> 00:06:15.563
They hurried to tell Matthew and Marilla.

102
00:06:15.583 --> 00:06:21.982
"Oh, Matthew," exclaimed Anne, "I've passed and I'm first—or one of the first.

103
00:06:22.662 --> 00:06:24.863
I'm not vain, but I'm thankful."

104
00:06:24.883 --> 00:06:29.566
"Well now, I've always said it," said Matthew, gazing at the list happily.

105
00:06:29.586 --> 00:06:31.907
"I knew you could beat them all."

106
00:06:32.487 --> 00:06:38.110
"You've done pretty well, I must say, Anne," said Marilla, trying to hide her extreme pride.

107
00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:40.091
"We're all proud of you."
